** - OK\\n151-\\n152-### Code examples\\n153-\\n154-#### Example\\n155-\\n156-**Request:**\\n--\\n970:## List runner applications for a repository\\n971-\\n972-```\\n973-GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/actions/runners/downloads\\n974-```\\n975-\\n976-Lists binaries for the runner application that you can download and run.\\n977-Authenticated users must have admin access to the repository to use this endpoint.\\n978-OAuth app tokens and personal access tokens (classic) need the repo scope to use this endpoint.\\n979-\\n980-### Parameters\\n981-\\n982-#### Headers\\n983-\\n984-* **`accept`** (string)\\n985-  Setting to `application/vnd.github+json` is recommended.\\n986-\\n987-#### Path and query parameters\\n988-\\n989-* **`owner`** (string) (required)\\n990-  The account owner of the repository. The name is not case sensitive.\\n991-\\n992-* **`repo`** (string) (required)\\n993-  The name of the repository without the .git extension. The name is not case sensitive.\\n994-\\n995-### HTTP response status codes\\n996-\\n997-* **200** - OK\\n998-\\n999-### Code examples\\n1000-\\n--\\n1013:Same response schema as [List runner applications for an organization](#list-runner-applications-for-an-organization).\\n1014-\\n1015-## Create configuration for a just-in-time runner for a repository\\n1016-\\n1017-```\\n1018-POST /repos/{owner}/{repo}/actions/runners/generate-jitconfig\\n1019-```\\n1020-\\n1021-Generates a configuration that can be passed to the runner application at startup.\\n1022-The authenticated user must have admin access to the repository.\\n1023-OAuth tokens and personal access tokens (classic) need therepo scope to use this endpoint.\\n1024-\\n1025-### Parameters\\n1026-\\n1027-#### Headers\\n1028-\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 2420,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 605,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
