{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000da2d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a87b-9700-7b13-a5a9-4a460ed866b3"},"sequence":2929,"recorded_at":1780531400005853,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"729941af-ea8e-4d7f-a339-63c28c483dc7","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"729941af-ea8e-4d7f-a339-63c28c483dc7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"729941af-ea8e-4d7f-a339-63c28c483dc7"},"call_id":"call_01a0a88ca46677e7ac3dd8eb41b6a879","text":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 32-34\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-4. **Checksum availability** — GitHub's downloads endpoint documents\n-   `sha256_checksum`, so the installer now fails closed: a missing/empty\n-   checksum throws `integrityMismatch` instead of skipping verification.\n+4. **Checksum availability (F1)** — GitHub's downloads endpoint documents\n+   `sha256_checksum`, so the installer now fails closed: a missing/empty\n+   checksum throws `integrityMismatch` instead of skipping verification.\n+5. **HTTP 204 rejected (F2)** — `PUT …/runner-groups/{id}/repositories`\n+   answers `204 No Content` in production, but the client accepted only\n+   200/201, failing every production repo-access update. `send()` now accepts\n+   204; only the two body-ignoring PUTs can legally return it.\n+6. **Post-config token retention (F6)** — when the follow-up runner-ID lookup\n+   failed after a successful `config.sh`, the single-use registration token\n+   stayed in Keychain. The token is now deleted immediately after config\n+   succeeds (it is consumed at that point), before any follow-up API call.\n","edit_facts":{"tool_name":"edit_file","path":"/tmp/TASK-260916-13diw4_outcome.md","added":11,"removed":3},"correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"edit_file","outcome":"success"}}}
