{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000dcf3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a87b-9700-7b13-a5a9-4a460ed866b3"},"sequence":3284,"recorded_at":1780531400006563,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"729941af-ea8e-4d7f-a339-63c28c483dc7","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"729941af-ea8e-4d7f-a339-63c28c483dc7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"729941af-ea8e-4d7f-a339-63c28c483dc7"},"terminal":"completed","text":"The new-runner wizard work is ready for review — handed off to review with board status `to-review` and checklist 19/19.\n\nWhat this run delivered, on top of the staged wizard already in the worktree: all four review-focus gaps plus all six demonstrated failures from the prior Astra rev1 verdict (F1–F6, `repeat-of: none`). Dedicated groups now send `allows_public_repositories: true` on create and PATCH it on adopted groups; `config --replace` is conditional on an explicit toggle with a pre-token remote-duplicate guard; same-name groups require a local ownership record or explicit takeover consent; the installer fails closed on missing checksums; the client accepts production `204` on the repos PUT; and the single-use registration token is deleted immediately after `config.sh` succeeds so a post-config API failure can't retain it.\n\nVerification observed in this session: CI gate `swift test --package-path Packages/RunnerControlCore` exit 0 with 110 tests passing; Xcode core suite exit 0; app target builds with only one pre-existing Sendable warning on an untouched line. AC coverage is 8 of 8 rows driven through production entry points (`RunnerRegistration.Flow.apply`, the API client, the installer, cross-checked by `RunnerDiscovery`), and 12 of 13 narrowing mutants were killed by named tests — the one survivor (M9, client default) is bounded in the report, with M9b killing the true Flow call-site gate. Candidate left uncommitted in the story worktree as required; full evidence, mutant table, and stated bounds are in `TASK-260916-13diw4_outcome_v2.md` on the board.","reason":null}}
